                  <provenance type="#m"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_198">Eton, Buckinghamshire.
                        Royal College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Contains the annotations of Robert Elyot, fellow of Eton from
                        c. 1474 until his death in January 1499 (BRUO 638). He was a prolific
                        annotator of books at Eton. Five are particularly heavily marked and were
                        probably his own, subsequently given to the college: MSS 17, 18, 34, 36, 76.
                        (His marks were discussed by N. R. Ker in The Library, 5th ser. 30 (1975),
                        233--7, with an addendum by R. Beadle in The Library, 5th ser. 32 (1977),
                        371--2.) His typical heads in the margins, fols. 144r, 146r, 193r, 204v,
                        205r. Cf. MS. 17.</p></provenance>
               </history>
